<%# locals: (scope:, sweep:, checked:, others: false) %>
<%# What a Filing rule would do to the unfiled bank transactions that are already there, which it can do when it's saved: how many it fits, and a box to file or ignore them the same way now, ticked to start with. Saving a rule from the filing form sweeps only the other ones, which went the same way as the one being filed. A bank transaction that a more specific rule is the one to file isn't counted, and is said so, since "no other fit" wouldn't be true. With none to file there's no box. The sentences are the helper's. %>
<% headline, leftover = sweep_sentences(sweep, others: others) %>
<p class="<%= "text-base-content/70" if sweep.count.zero? %>"><%= headline %></p>
<% if leftover %>
  <p class="text-base-content/70"><%= leftover %></p>
<% end %>
<% if sweep.count.positive? %>
  <%= fields_for scope, FilingRulesHelper::SweepChoice.new(sweep: checked) do |sweep_form| %>
    <%= render "components/field", form: sweep_form, attribute: :sweep, control: :checkbox, label: "File or ignore them the same way now",
          hint: (others ? "Only the ones that went the same way as this one." : nil) do |field| %>
      <%= sweep_form.check_box :sweep, **field %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
